                    {
                        "sense_id": "e308c45e-0503-3c81-a571-1c713699db2a",
                        "entry_id": "87c47096-937d-376d-a03c-40a9222ff392",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Capable of being dug.",
                            "Possible and (especially) feasible to dig physically."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe400421-2b67-48e7-910e-b89344150bea",
                                "sense_id": "e308c45e-0503-3c81-a571-1c713699db2a",
                                "text": "The rocky soil was diggable, but only with difficulty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e8ee85e-b101-41a4-b168-d0b9009b1004",
                                "sense_id": "e308c45e-0503-3c81-a571-1c713699db2a",
                                "text": "Though there seemed to be some “diggable” places, Dr. Levinthal said that the project scientists “might decide to look around” for alternate sampling sites."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b62b9a0c-834e-411f-80ca-bad54cd62980",
                                "sense_id": "e308c45e-0503-3c81-a571-1c713699db2a",
                                "text": "Intriguingly, their idea also explains why gold and platinum are found in the Earth’s crust, well within diggable reach."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c1929df-60af-4cbe-802a-43a0aec8bbcb",
                                "sense_id": "e308c45e-0503-3c81-a571-1c713699db2a",
                                "text": "Two sloths have also died at the Las Vegas SeaQuest. Like all the others, it is located in an indoor shopping center, where natural light, humidity, vegetation and diggable floors — the environmental setting in which many animals thrive — are in short supply."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8eae3359-bfc5-3f81-ba1a-582b280af5a6",
                        "entry_id": "87c47096-937d-376d-a03c-40a9222ff392",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Capable of being dug.",
                            "Worthy of digging (appreciating and enjoying)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4053d7fe-5ad8-446b-a405-baa08889c678",
                                "sense_id": "8eae3359-bfc5-3f81-ba1a-582b280af5a6",
                                "text": "Near-synonyms: appreciable, enjoyable"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2bfd731-7d78-4df7-b513-318343b4da60",
                                "sense_id": "8eae3359-bfc5-3f81-ba1a-582b280af5a6",
                                "text": "Yeah, their jazz is diggable, but they leave something on the table by not getting funkier with the horns."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
